  "nl_text": "This database schema is named rschema_0333 and it is designed to store and manage user-related data. It contains 6 tables: User, User_homepage, User_connection_request_record, User_connection_establishment_record, Feed, and User_homepage_join.\nThe User table stores user-specific information such as their address, birthday, current location, email, gender, hometown, interests, motto, name, password, personal profile, phone number, relationship status, user ID, user type, and username. The User_ID is the primary key for this table.\nThe User_homepage table stores information about a user's homepage such as the creation time, homepage ID, introduction, title, and the User_ID. The User_ID is a foreign key referencing the User table.\nThe User_connection_request_record table stores information about connection requests. It records the receiver user ID, record ID, send time, and sender user ID. The receiver_user_ID and sender_user_ID are foreign keys referencing the User table.\nThe User_connection_establishment_record table stores information about established connections. It records the connection time, receiver ID, record ID, and sender ID. Both receiver_ID and sender_ID are foreign keys referencing the User table.\nThe Feed table stores information about user feeds. It includes feed ID, feed content, homepage ID, post time, and user ID. The homepage_ID is a foreign key referencing the User_homepage table, and the user_ID is a foreign key referencing the User table.\nFinally, the User_homepage_join table stores information about when users join a homepage. It includes homepage ID, join time, and user ID. The homepage_ID is a foreign key referencing the User_homepage table, and the user_ID is a foreign key referencing the User table. The combination of join_time, homepage_ID, and user_ID forms the primary key of this table.\nThis schema ensures data integrity by enforcing primary keys and foreign keys, and by defining constraints on the columns to maintain entity integrity. It also allows for referential integrity, as changes to the User table are cascaded to related tables.",
  "gold_question": "Description of Social Network System Requirements: For user registration and login, users can register and log in to the system using username and password. The system supports different types of users, such as regular users and administrators. For personal information management, users can fill in and manage basic personal information, including name, phone, address, email, birthday, gender, relationship status, interests, etc., and can edit detailed information such as personal profile, motto, hometown, and current location. For user connection management, users can establish connections with other users, and the system records the connection time. Users can send and receive connection requests, and the system records the request sending time. For user homepage management, users can create personal homepages, including title, introduction, and creation time. Other users can join user's homepage and the joining time is recorded. For homepage feed management, users can post updates on their own homepage, including text content, and the posting time is recorded. Other users can also post updates on user's homepage, creating interaction. For the functionality of users joining multiple homepages, users can join multiple different homepages, and the joining time is recorded. The system supports associations between users and multiple homepages.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0333.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0333\nCREATE TABLE `User` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `hometown` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `current_location` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `birthday` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `relationship_status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `interests` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `motto` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `personal_profile` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `user_type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_homepage` (\n  `homepage_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `introduction` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `creation_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`homepage_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `User_homepage_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_connection_request_record` (\n  `record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sender_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `receiver_user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `send_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`record_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `User_connection_request_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sender_user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `User_connection_request_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`receiver_user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_connection_establishment_record` (\n  `record_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sender_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `receiver_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `connection_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`record_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `User_connection_establishment_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`sender_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `User_connection_establishment_record_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`receiver_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Feed` (\n  `feed_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `homepage_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `feed_content` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `post_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`feed_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `Feed_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `Feed_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`homepage_id`) REFERENCES `User_homepage` (`homepage_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `User_homepage_join` (\n  `homepage_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `join_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`join_time`, `homepage_id`, `user_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `User_homepage_join_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`homepage_id`) REFERENCES `User_homepage` (`homepage_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `User_homepage_join_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`user_id`) REFERENCES `User` (`user_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
